The skeletons sink into the green slurry, their lower limbs dissolving on contact. The air elementalist conjures a panicked updraft to lift his upper torso out of the vat, but I clap my hands, slamming two granite slabs together to crush his skull to dust. The others submerge completely, their bones hissing and melting into sludge.

