Blind in the boiling mist, I try locking onto their positions with magical sense alone. A sharp crackle pops at point-blank range, and before I can react, an explosion tears through my wards, throwing me into the cobblestones.

Two ribs snap on impact. My breath locks in my chest. Before I can raise a hand or roll aside, a massive slab of granite slams down from above, crushing my body flat against the pavement.

}
