"And entertainment is what I'm after, Barry!" Hadrik laughs, keeping the chain spinning. "I might make this part of my daily morning routine. Though I should check with our guest first—wouldn't want to be rude. What do you say, Arraka? Does ten in the morning work for your daily spin?"

"Dwarf!" Arraka's shrieking voice wobbles with nausea from the blur of gold. "When I get out, I'm reaching down your gullet, turning you inside out, and hanging you from an oak by your own intestines as a tree swing!"

