ID: Ch11b-Hole
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch11_casualties,1) if (v_agility == 4 && v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4)
set(v_ch11_saved_rose,0) if (v_hearing == 4 && v_perception < 4 || v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4 && v_agility < 4 || v_hearing < 4)
set(v_ch11_saved_rose,1) if (v_agility == 4 && v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4)
achievement("No casualties",v_ac_ch11_casualties)
#if(v_hearing < 4) {
 

A sharp, violent crunch of fracturing stone echoes from the far edge of the square. I spin toward the sound, and the breath dies in my throat.

A ragged hole gapes in the cobblestones near the fruit stalls. Rose stands frozen in front of it, arms hanging limp, eyes wide and unseeing. Wrapped around her back is a newly risen skeleton, locking her in a tight grip while plunging a rusted iron blade deep through her chest. The color drains from Rose's face in a heartbeat. As her knees buckle, the skeleton twists the hilt one final time, crumbling to dry bone meal as her body collapses onto the cold pavement.

"Rose!" Daren roars, sprinting across the plaza.

He drops hard onto his knees beside her, hands blazing with frantic white radiance. Pulse after pulse of healing light pours into her torn chest, but the flesh stays cold, the wound refusing to knit. We gather in stunned silence around them as Daren channels every shred of his mana into her motionless frame, while Rose stares blankly at the sky, her pulse gone.

"Rose, stay with me!" Daren shouts, his voice cracking into a ragged sob.

}
#if(v_hearing == 4 && v_perception < 4) {
 

A faint grinding of subterranean stone catches my ear from across the plaza. I turn toward the sound, spotting Rose standing near the far storefronts.

Before my eyes can pick out the danger, the cobblestones beneath her boots erupt in a shower of mortar and shattered stone. A skeleton claws out of the earth, plunging a rusted iron dagger straight through her sternum. Rose stiffens, a gasp catching in her throat before her expression turns completely blank. Her fingers go limp. As the light leaves her eyes, the skeleton twists the blade, disintegrating into gray bone meal as Rose falls backward onto the stones.

"Rose!" Daren roars, sprinting across the square.

He drops hard onto his knees beside her, hands blazing with frantic white radiance. Pulse after pulse of healing light pours into her torn chest, but the flesh stays cold, the wound refusing to knit. We gather in stunned silence around them as Daren channels every shred of his mana into her motionless frame, while Rose stares blankly at the sky, her pulse gone.

"Rose, stay with me!" Daren shouts, his voice cracking into a ragged sob.

}
#if(v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4 && v_agility < 4) {
 

A faint grinding of subterranean stone catches my ear from across the plaza. I turn toward the sound and spot hairline fissures spidering across the mortar beneath Rose's boots. Instinct screams danger. Before my mind catches up, I sprint across the square.

I am ten paces out when the pavement detonates. A skeleton claws upward from the fissure, driving a rusted dagger straight through Rose's heart. Shock flickers across her face, then dissolves into hollow numbness as her arms drop limp. The skeleton twists the hilt, disintegrating into gray powder as Rose falls backward onto the cold stones.

"Rose!" Daren roars, sprinting past me.

He crashes onto his knees beside her, hands blazing with desperate white light. He layers heal after heal into her chest, but the wound stays open, the blood pooling dark against the cobblestones. We surround them in stunned silence while Daren channels every shred of power into her heart, but Rose stares blankly at the clouds, her chest completely still.

"Rose, stay with me!" Daren shouts, voice breaking into a sob.

It is useless. Daren knows it as well as I do. Her chest is still. Her pulse stopped before she hit the stones. After everything we endured to bring her safely home to Thilias, she died in seconds. And even the legendary healer cannot mend an extinguished soul.

"No..." Kate's voice trembles in furious denial. "This isn't real. It's another illusion! The necromancer couldn't touch her—the tournament protections would have struck him down! This is a trick!"

"The necromancer is dead," Illuna says quietly. "The tournament wards linked to his person dissolved the moment his aura died. The sacrificial curse was crafted specifically to execute after his death to bypass the rule. A loophole. This is no illusion. Rose is gone."

"No!" Kate's eyes brim with tears. "She can't just die! It isn't fair! She didn't deserve this!"

Kate presses the heels of her hands against her eyes, fighting a sob that wracks her shoulders.

"She didn't deserve this..." she whispers.

"My fault..." Daren murmurs, his hands dropping limp from Rose's chest. "I offered to escort her. I gave my word she would be safe. I failed her."

"Hold on, Daren," Hadrik says softly. "You can't carry that. Rose knew the danger when she chose to stand with us yesterday after the noble. She made her choice and stood by it to the end. She died with honor, and we should respect that."

"What do you know about Rose?!" Daren detonates, whirling on the dwarf with blazing eyes. "You think she wanted to die in the gutter of this cesspool?! You think she died proud, knowing she left two young siblings behind with no one to care for them?! Do you measure every tragedy by your primitive warrior nonsense?! What gives you the right to talk about her like that?!"

}
#if(v_agility == 4 && v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4) {
 

A faint grinding of subterranean stone catches my ear from across the plaza. I turn and spot hairline fissures spidering across the mortar beneath Rose's boots. Instinct screams danger. My body moves on pure reflex, boosted agility propelling me across the square in a blur of speed.

The cobblestones erupt into the air as a skeleton claws out of the ground, lunging with a rusted iron blade aimed straight for Rose's heart.

I dive through the shower of mortar, wrapping both hands around the skeleton's neck and slamming it into the ground before the blade reaches her. I draw my dagger to finish it, but the impact against the stones shatters the brittle construct into harmless bone splinters.

"Rose, are you hurt?!" Daren shouts, sprinting over with the rest of the party.

"I... no!" Rose gasps, clutching her chest against the wall. "Barry caught it!"

"How did you spot that?" Kate asks, looking at the pulverized bones. "Did the device trigger a premonition?"

"No," I say, catching my breath as my boots skid on the loose gravel. "I heard the stone grinding and saw the crack before it struck."

"I don't understand," Kate says. "Why did the trap trigger at all? Wouldn't tournament protection block the skeleton from touching Rose?"

"No," Illuna explains. "When the necromancer died, the tournament ward bound to his soul vanished with his aura. The sacrificial curse was designed to fire after death to exploit that exact loophole. He intended to assassinate her posthumously."

"Gods..." Rose whispers, her face pale. "I had no idea magic could be twisted like that. To go to such lengths just to kill me..."

"You did rewind the universe five minutes ago," Hadrik notes with a grin. "How did you manage that trick, anyway?"

"I don't know," Rose says, shaking her head. "Eiden called me a time weaver earlier, but I thought he was mocking me. I had no idea how to trigger it. I was just so desperate to undo what happened that it tore out of me. I don't know if I can ever do it again."

"Once was plenty," Daren says, exhaling slowly. "You didn't just save our lives—you may have saved Varathia. But we can analyze it later. Right now, let me mend these wounds before another pair of bounty hunters ambushes us."

As Daren's white healing light settles over our injuries, a massive, echoing chime reverberates across the heavens.

}
#if(v_hearing <= 4 && v_perception < 4 || v_hearing < 4) {
It is useless. Daren knows it as well as I do. Her chest is still. Her pulse stopped before she hit the stones. After everything we endured to bring her safely home to Thilias, she died in seconds. And even the legendary healer cannot mend an extinguished soul.

"No..." Kate's voice trembles in furious denial. "This isn't real. It's another illusion! The necromancer couldn't touch her—the tournament protections would have struck him down! This is a trick!"

"The necromancer is dead," Illuna says quietly. "The tournament wards linked to his person dissolved the moment his aura died. The sacrificial curse was crafted specifically to execute after his death to bypass the rule. A loophole. This is no illusion. Rose is gone."

"No!" Kate's eyes brim with tears. "She can't just die! It isn't fair! She didn't deserve this!"

Kate presses the heels of her hands against her eyes, fighting a sob that wracks her shoulders.

"She didn't deserve this..." she whispers.

"My fault..." Daren murmurs, his hands dropping limp from Rose's chest. "I offered to escort her. I gave my word she would be safe. I failed her."

"Hold on, Daren," Hadrik says softly. "You can't carry that. Rose knew the danger when she chose to stand with us yesterday after the noble. She made her choice and stood by it to the end. She died with honor, and we should respect that."

"What do you know about Rose?!" Daren detonates, whirling on the dwarf with blazing eyes. "You think she wanted to die in the gutter of this cesspool?! You think she died proud, knowing she left two young siblings behind with no one to care for them?! Do you measure every tragedy by your primitive warrior nonsense?! What gives you the right to talk about her like that?!"

}
choice("Continue", Ch11b-Revenant, v_current_scene = Ch11b-Revenant) if (v_hearing == 4 && v_perception < 4 || v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4 && v_agility < 4 || v_hearing < 4)
choice("Continue", Ch11b-Ending, v_current_scene = Ch11b-Ending) if (v_agility == 4 && v_hearing == 4 && v_perception == 4)


ID: Ch11b-Revenant
TEXT:

Rose's corpse stirs. Slowly, stiffly, she raises her torso from the cobblestones, staring ahead with empty, glassy eyes. Her aura feels hollow and freezing, void of warmth, and her skin has turned the color of chalk.

"Rose!" Kate gasps, taking a step forward. "You're alive!"

"No," Daren says, his voice flat and dark. "That isn't Rose."

"What are you saying?" Kate demands. "She's right there!"

"Only the shell," Illuna says coldly. "Rose is dead. What sits before us is a revenant—an undead construct possessing the host's memories but bound to a new will. That is why the necromancer cast a sacrificial curse before his death. To harvest the time weaver's vessel for his god."

"No, that's impossible!" Kate's voice cracks as Rose stands and begins walking away. "Rose, tell them it isn't true!"

"The one you called Rose is gone," the revenant speaks without looking back, her voice flat and hollow. "I serve Ulruk, the God of Death. My task is to deliver this time weaver vessel safely to his altar."

"You won't take a single step," Daren snarls, drawing his broadsword. "You leave her body here for a proper burial."

"You cannot stop me, healer," the revenant says, continuing her slow stride across the stones. "Unlike your friend, I command this power. I need only freeze time for a few hours, and to your eyes, I will have vanished across the continent. My master awaits."

She walks onward, ignoring our presence as if we were dust beneath her boots. Daren stands frozen, sword trembling in his grip, torn between duty and the face of the woman he failed to save.

At the edge of the square, the revenant pauses and turns her head. For a fraction of a second, the glassy vacancy in her eyes breaks, replaced by a flicker of deep, aching sorrow.

"Take care of the children for me," she whispers. "I don't think I'll be coming back to that house..."

"Stop!" Daren roars.

He lunges forward, blade flashing in a desperate arc, but the air blurs and she vanishes before steel meets flesh. The sword cleaves empty space.

We stand in the hollow silence of the market square as a booming chime reverberates across the heavens.

choice("Continue", Ch11b-Ending, v_current_scene = Ch11b-Ending)


ID: Ch11b-Ending
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch11_average,1) if (v_available_points == 19)
achievement("Average Joe",v_ac_ch11_average)
Colossal light-castings ignite across the morning sky, casting a brilliant azure glow over the rooftops of Thilias. Shutters creak open as frightened citizens peer out from their windows. Every screen displays the same scene: a wild-haired gnome in thick magnifying goggles and an oil-stained coat, humming cheerfully while twisting copper wires in a cluttered workshop.

He pauses, pushes the goggles up onto his forehead, and presses his face against the scrying lens.

"How peculiar!" the gnome mutters, blinking at the feed. "How very peculiar! I could swear I've wired these conduits a thousand times, but the amber light never turned emerald until now. Well, no matter! Can everyone hear me out there?"

A low murmur ripples through the surrounding streets.

"Wait, what am I saying?" The gnome chuckles, tapping his temple. "One-way relay. Even if you shout, I won't hear a peep. Right, then! I'll read the official speech I jotted down on parchment, and if the feed fails, I'll just broadcast again tomorrow. Now where did that wretched sheet go?"

The gnome ducks beneath his workbench for several seconds while the town murmurs in confusion.

"Ah, well! Must have misplaced it!" He pops back up with an easy grin. "Improvisation it is!"

He clears his throat, puffing out his chest.

"Ladies and gentlemen! Or rather, gentlemen and gentlemen, given the unfortunate absence of female mages in our ranks! Welcome to the Magium tournament! I am Golmyck, King of Thilias, and I have a public announcement. First, an apology to every participant on Varathia. Upon arrival, you were meant to receive your directives privately, but the relay device suffered an immediate malfunction. I've spent the past week repairing the conduits, but given the delay, I am using this emergency broadcast to reach all major cities and wilderness sectors. If any participants are out of range, please pass along the word!"

Golmyck clears his throat once more, his grin widening across the sky.

"With pleasantries concluded," he proclaims, "the hour has arrived to deliver what you came for."

He beams at the lens.

"Your first objectives!"

-----End of book 1-----

choice("Proceed towards book 2", Ch11b-Credits, v_current_scene = Ch11b-Credits, v_first_book_purchased = 1)


ID: Ch11b-Credits
TEXT:

set(v_first_book_purchased,1)
set(v_iap_check_resume,1) if (v_iap_checked != 0 && v_iap_checked != 2)
set(v_iap_check_resume,0)
 This marks the end of the first Magium book.

The second book has been completed and is ready to unlock, but only the first eleven chapters of book 3 are available so far, with the next chapters to be released one by one, as I write them. (the main series will likely have 5 books in total)

My current estimate is that the 12th chapter of the third book should be released within the next few months.

If you already paid to unlock the 2nd book, you can tap on the button below to proceed. Otherwise, you will need to complete 25 achievements from the 1st book in order to unlock the second one.

You can see how many more achievements you need to complete in the achievements menu. 

I would also like to add that I strongly suggest you save the game now on a save slot you won't overwrite, if you're planning to start completing achievements, since otherwise you'll lose the progress of your current playthrough and you'll have to finish the game again in order to be able to progress to the next book.

You should also be careful to not uninstall the game, since all of the next books will be uploaded within the same app, and if you uninstall the game, all your local progress, including your achievements, will be lost.

Thank you for playing!

P.S. If you enjoyed the game, don't forget to recommend it to your friends. 

choice("Proceed to book 2", B2-Ch01a-Intro, v_b1_saved_stats = 1, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, special:checkpoint_save)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
